selector_to_html = {"a[href=\"#pyskyfire.network.engine_network.EngineNetwork.update\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.network.engine_network.EngineNetwork.update\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">update</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span> <span class=\"sig-return\"><span class=\"sig-return-icon\">\u2192</span> <span class=\"sig-return-typehint\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">float</span></a></span></span></dt><dd><p>Execute one full sweep over all blocks.</p><p>Calls each block\u2019s <code class=\"xref py py-meth docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">compute()</span></code> with the current <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">stations</span></code> /\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">signals</span></code>, merges its outputs, and tracks the maximum relative change\nacross all updated entries.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#pyskyfire.network.engine_network.EngineNetwork._toposort\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.network.engine_network.EngineNetwork._toposort\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">_toposort</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">blocks</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">Iterable</span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">[</span></span><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.network.blocks.Block</span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">]</span></span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span> <span class=\"sig-return\"><span class=\"sig-return-icon\">\u2192</span> <span class=\"sig-return-typehint\"><span class=\"pre\">List</span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">[</span></span><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.network.blocks.Block</span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">]</span></span></span></span></dt><dd><p>Compute an execution order for blocks.</p><p>The default implementation preserves the given order. Replace with a\ndependency-aware topological sort (e.g., Kahn\u2019s algorithm) using each\nblock\u2019s <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">station_*</span></code> and <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">signal_*</span></code> metadata for strict ordering.</p><p class=\"rubric\">Notes</p><p>Sorting is currently not implemented; the user is responsible for\nproviding a solvable order.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#pyskyfire.network.engine_network.EngineNetwork.run_fixed_point\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.network.engine_network.EngineNetwork.run_fixed_point\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">run_fixed_point</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">tol</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">float</span></a></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">1e-06</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">max_iter</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">int</span></a></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">100</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Iterate fixed-point sweeps until convergence or iteration cap.</p><p>Repeatedly calls <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#pyskyfire.network.engine_network.EngineNetwork.update\" title=\"pyskyfire.network.engine_network.EngineNetwork.update\"><code class=\"xref py py-meth docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">update()</span></code></a> until the maximum relative residual falls\nbelow <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">tol</span></code> or until <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">max_iter</span></code> sweeps have been performed.</p><p class=\"rubric\">Notes</p><p>Appends per-iteration residuals to <code class=\"xref py py-attr docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">residuals</span></code>. On convergence,\nperforms a post-process sweep calling each block\u2019s <code class=\"xref py py-meth docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">post_process()</span></code>\nand stores any non-empty results in <code class=\"xref py py-attr docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">block_results</span></code>.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#pyskyfire.network.engine_network.EngineNetwork\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.network.engine_network.EngineNetwork\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.network.engine_network.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">EngineNetwork</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">stations</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">Dict</span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">[</span></span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">str</span></a><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">,</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"Station.html#pyskyfire.network.engine_network.Station\" title=\"pyskyfire.network.engine_network.Station\"><span class=\"pre\">Station</span></a><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">]</span></span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">signals</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">Dict</span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">[</span></span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">str</span></a><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">,</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">float</span></a><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">]</span></span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">blocks</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">List</span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">[</span></span><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.network.blocks.Block</span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">]</span></span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Fixed-point engine network orchestrating stations and signals.</p><p>The network manages two dictionaries:</p><p>Blocks added to the network advertise four metadata lists\n(<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">station_inputs</span></code>, <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">station_outputs</span></code>, <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">signal_inputs</span></code>, <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">signal_outputs</span></code>)\nand implement <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">compute(stations,</span> <span class=\"pre\">signals)</span> <span class=\"pre\">-&gt;</span> <span class=\"pre\">(stations_out,</span> <span class=\"pre\">signals_out)</span></code>.\nThe network executes blocks in a chosen order and applies a fixed-point\niteration until convergence.</p><p class=\"rubric\">Notes</p><p>The default execution order preserves the given block list. A dependency-\naware topological sort can replace it; see <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#pyskyfire.network.engine_network.EngineNetwork._toposort\" title=\"pyskyfire.network.engine_network.EngineNetwork._toposort\"><code class=\"xref py py-meth docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">_toposort()</span></code></a>.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#pyskyfire.network.engine_network.EngineNetwork._merge_and_residual\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.network.engine_network.EngineNetwork._merge_and_residual\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">_merge_and_residual</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">store</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">Dict</span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">[</span></span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">str</span></a><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">,</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">Any</span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">]</span></span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">delta</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">Dict</span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">[</span></span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">str</span></a><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">,</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">Any</span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">]</span></span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">res</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">float</span></a></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span> <span class=\"sig-return\"><span class=\"sig-return-icon\">\u2192</span> <span class=\"sig-return-typehint\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">float</span></a></span></span></dt><dd><p>Merge updates into a store and track the max relative residual.</p><p>For each key in <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">delta</span></code>:</p><p class=\"rubric\">Notes</p><p>To avoid division by zero, denominators are clamped with small epsilons:\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">1e-10</span></code> for stations and <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">1e-8</span></code> for scalars. If either <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">mdot</span></code> is\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">NaN</span></code>, the mass-flow term is skipped for that key.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"Station.html#pyskyfire.network.engine_network.Station\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.network.engine_network.Station\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.network.engine_network.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">Station</span></span></dt><dd><p>Thermodynamic state container used by the engine network.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#pyskyfire-network-engine-network-enginenetwork\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">pyskyfire.network.engine_network.EngineNetwork<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#pyskyfire-network-engine-network-enginenetwork\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1>"}
skip_classes = ["headerlink", "sd-stretched-link"]

window.onload = function () {
    for (const [select, tip_html] of Object.entries(selector_to_html)) {
        const links = document.querySelectorAll(` ${select}`);
        for (const link of links) {
            if (skip_classes.some(c => link.classList.contains(c))) {
                continue;
            }

            tippy(link, {
                content: tip_html,
                allowHTML: true,
                arrow: true,
                placement: 'auto-start', maxWidth: 600, interactive: false,
                onShow(instance) {MathJax.typesetPromise([instance.popper]).then(() => {});},
            });
        };
    };
    console.log("tippy tips loaded!");
};
